## 🌸 English Contemplation

Knowledge becomes spiritually meaningful only when it ripens into discernment.

Discernment reveals the impermanence of everything that changes. From that clarity arises dispassion—not rejection of life, but freedom from demanding permanence from the impermanent.

True dispassion then matures into surrender.

Surrender is not defeat. It is the ending of the illusion that the ego independently governs life.

And when surrender becomes steady, the seeker discovers that the Truth to which he was surrendering was never separate from his own deepest Self.

### **Knowledge informs.  
Discernment clarifies.  
Dispassion releases.  
Surrender dissolves.  
Self-knowledge rests in what has always been.**

